Description: tiny-voca-ru, the Russian tiny-voca model
 tiny-voca-ru (egnch/tiny-voca-ru, Apache-2.0) is the tiny-voca
 architecture trained on Russian.  The new family tiny_voca_ru runs on the
 tiny_voca runtime with a port of the model's rule-based frontend (clean,
 lexicon, g2p, tokenizer) for stressed ("+" or U+0301), normalised text.
 tiny_voca: the phonemes and vowels come from the config ("phones",
 "vowels") when it has them, the phonemizer section is optional, and the
 assets loader takes the family name.
 Checked against the Python package: the same tokens on 1514 of 1517 test
 lines (the other 3 it refuses), equal durations and a median waveform
 error of 4.5e-4 of the peak on 190 utterances.
Author: Grigory Tuboltsev
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
